From 43b2d1d1b09a8d21e4137b5a947f907243cb2d21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Riddhi Parekh <riddhi.parekh@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 10:05:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iKVM: PCIe EP local display and remote KVM support for i.MX95

PCIe EP drivers (pci-imx6, pci-epf-test, pci-epf-core):
- Set EP device class to Display (VGA), BAR4 for DPU95 registers
- BAR2: 32MB VRAM for host-driven framebuffer streaming (~60 FPS)
- /dev/stream char device (mmap/ioctl) for userspace access
- DMA-BUF export, EDID via BAR1, dynamic resolution support
- DT-based VRAM mapping via ioremap_wc()

DRM/DPU95:
- Dedicated VRAM pool via of_reserved_mem_device_init()
- STRIDE_OVERRIDE plane property for iKVM display
- DRM_IMX_DPU_GET_DMA_ADDRESS ioctl for GEM buffer access

media: stream2v4l2:
- V4L2 capture driver exposing PCIe host console for obmc-ikvm

DTS:
- VRAM reserved memory node (64MB at 0x94000000)
- PCIe EP DTB generation, 4K display via lt9611uxc MIPI-HDMI
- lt9611uxc: EDID_NUM_BLOCKS=4 for Dell 4K monitors

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Riddhi Parekh <riddhi.parekh@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: Shreyash Damanwala <shreyash.damanwala@nxp.com>
Signed-off-by: Disha Das <disha.das@nxp.com>
